<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nestor Lakoba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor">Nestor</a> Lakoba was an Abkhaz Bolshevik who led Soviet Abkhazia from 1921 until his death in 1936. Close to Stalin, he slowed collectivisation and protected local landowners and customs, but saw Abkhazia reduced to an autonomous republic within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in 1931. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a> in December 1936 after a dinner with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavrentiy-beria">Lavrentiy Beria</a>, probably poisoned, and was then denounced as an enemy of the people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nestor-lakoba.jpg" alt="Nestor Lakoba" width="280" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lakoba_Nestor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
